grading systems.

24
00:02:08.978 --> 00:02:16.862
g. , AI ethics board, compliance officer,
developers) to accountability

25
00:02:16.862 --> 00:02:17.650
responsibilities.

26
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:25.009
Follow every arrow in order and name the state
before and after each transition.

27
00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:30.806
The trace converts an abstract statement into
an inspectable sequence.

28
00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:37.693
Name each dependency explicitly, and keep
labels and representations consistent

29
00:02:37.693 --> 00:02:39.759
throughout the analysis.

30
00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:47.416
Next, compare the choices involved in Map
Phase: Context and Impacts and make the

31
00:02:47.416 --> 00:02:49.034
decision criteria explicit.

32
00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:56.441
Map documents context, intended use, affected
people, and potential impacts.

33
00:02:56.441 --> 00:03:03.222
Consider this worked case: A self-driving car
manufacturer maps the operational design

34
00:03:03.222 --> 00:03:09.438
domain, specifying weather conditions and
traffic scenarios where the system will

35
00:03:09.438 --> 00:03:10.003
operate.

36
00:03:10.003 --> 00:03:17.088
Compare alternatives against the same
constraints so the evaluation does not move

37
00:03:17.088 --> 00:03:18.269
the goalposts.

38
00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:25.159
Using shared criteria turns a preference into
a defensible technical choice.

39
00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:32.082
Name each dependency explicitly, and keep
labels and representations consistent

40
00:03:32.082 --> 00:03:34.159
throughout the analysis.

41
00:03:34.274 --> 00:03:42.018
Apply Measure Phase: Risk Analysis Methods to
a worked situation instead of treating it as

42
00:03:42.018 --> 00:03:43.567
an isolated definition.

43
00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:50.599
Measure uses qualitative and quantitative
methods to analyze identified risks.

44
00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:57.784
Consider this worked case: Researchers conduct
A/B testing and statistical analysis to

45
00:03:57.784 --> 00:04:04.968
measure the fairness and accuracy of a facial
recognition model across different

46
00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:05.567
demographics.

47
00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:14.390
g. , stakeholder interviews), right side shows
quantitative metrics (e. g. , accuracy, bias

48
00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:15.020
scores).

49
00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:22.418
Work from the concrete inputs to the result,
checking units, types, or invariants at each

50
00:04:22.418 --> 00:04:22.911
step.

51
00:04:22.911 --> 00:04:28.067
The worked case shows both how to apply the
method and how to check it.

52
00:04:28.178 --> 00:04:35.102
Examine the tradeoffs in Manage Phase:
Prioritization and Monitoring, including what

53
00:04:35.102 --> 00:04:38.878
improves and what becomes more difficult.

54
00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:46.081
Manage prioritizes risks and allocates
resources for response and monitoring.

55
00:04:46.081 --> 00:04:53.297
Consider this worked case: A financial
institution prioritizes high-risk algorithmic

56
00:04:53.297 --> 00:05:01.234
trading models for continuous monitoring and
allocates resources for real-time anomaly

57
00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:01.956
detection.

58
00:05:01.956 --> 00:05:08.987
State the benefit, the cost, and the condition
under which the tradeoff is acceptable.

59
00:05:08.987 --> 00:05:16.424
Making the tradeoff visible prevents a local
improvement from hiding a larger cost.

60
00:05:16.538 --> 00:05:22.142
Stress-test the reasoning around Machine
Learning Workflows: Supervised vs.

61
00:05:22.142 --> 00:05:29.613
Unsupervised with an edge case and identify
which assumption controls the outcome.

62
00:05:29.613 --> 00:05:35.581
Supervised methods learn a mapping from
examples paired with target labels.

63
00:05:35.581 --> 00:05:44.235
Consider this worked case: A spam filter uses
supervised learning with labeled email data,

64
00:05:44.235 --> 00:05:50.416
whereas customer segmentation uses
unsupervised clustering to group users by

65
00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.034
behavior.

66
00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:57.612
Change one assumption at a time and observe
which part of the reasoning no longer holds.

67
00:05:57.612 --> 00:06:04.753
The edge case reveals the boundary of the
claim without discarding the useful core idea.

68
00:06:04.874 --> 00:06:12.465
Use Preprocessing and Leakage Prevention to
diagnose a failure by separating symptoms,

69
00:06:12.465 --> 00:06:14.995
causes, and corrective action.

70
00:06:14.995 --> 00:06:21.995
Preprocessing must be fitted only on permitted
training data to avoid leakage.

71
00:06:21.995 --> 00:06:29.487
Consider this worked case: A medical imaging
pipeline standardizes image dimensions and

72
00:06:29.487 --> 00:06:36.355
normalizes pixel values using only the
training set statistics before validation.

73
00:06:36.355 --> 00:06:43.946
Locate the first point where observed behavior
diverges from expected behavior, then test the

74
00:06:43.946 --> 00:06:45.573
smallest plausible cause.

75
00:06:45.573 --> 00:06:52.667
The diagnosis is strongest when another person
can reproduce the observation and the test.

76
00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:59.057
Connect Cross-Validation and Evaluation
Metrics to the earlier ideas and explain how

77
00:06:59.057 --> 00:07:02.196
the pieces work as one system.

78
00:07:02.196 --> 00:07:08.571
Evaluation metrics must match the task and the
cost of different errors.

79
00:07:08.571 --> 00:07:16.149
Consider this worked case: A fraud detection
system uses k-fold cross-validation to assess

80
00:07:16.149 --> 00:07:23.144
model stability, with precision and recall
metrics weighted to penalize false negatives

81
00:07:23.144 --> 00:07:23.727
heavily.

82
00:07:23.728 --> 00:07:33.357
Explain each connection explicitly and verify
that information retains the same meaning

83
00:07:33.357 --> 00:07:34.962
across representations.

84
00:07:34.962 --> 00:07:42.118
The synthesis matters only if every connection
remains supported by the original evidence.

85
00:07:42.242 --> 00:07:48.796
Finish with Practical Analysis Checklist for
AI Deployment as a practical checklist that

86
00:07:48.796 --> 00:07:51.317
can guide a new analysis.

87
00:07:51.317 --> 00:07:59.207
It also considers robustness, privacy,
security, transparency, and fairness.

88
00:07:59.207 --> 00:08:06.554
Consider this worked case: A deployment
checklist verifies that the AI system

89
00:08:06.554 --> 00:08:13.289
maintains fairness thresholds, logs privacy
compliance, and updates monitoring alerts when

90
00:08:13.289 --> 00:08:15.738
distribution shift is detected.

91
00:08:15.738 --> 00:08:23.971
For each checklist item, record the evidence,
the remaining uncertainty, and the next

92
00:08:23.971 --> 00:08:25.238
verification step.

93
00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:32.151
The result is a repeatable procedure, not a
conclusion that depends on memory or

94
00:08:32.151 --> 00:08:32.645
intuition.
